  "version": "32.5",
  "rules": {
    "hero": "1920x440 WebP",
    "neanderthalReconstruction": "1024x1024 WebP",
    "speciesMedia": "Species-specific specimen/cast/reconstruction media; each item carries source + license metadata",
    "commonAncestor": "Original schematic; not a recovered species portrait",
    "externalMediaPolicy": "All built-in production media is self-hosted. Real media enters through the CMS with source and rights metadata.",
    "architecture": "Production UI references active canonical media records. Legacy assets have an explicit migration disposition and are not shipped. Canonical media carries provenance/rights metadata, explicit roles/variants and research subject typing. The Explorer client consumes only a frozen server-built read model. Phase 2 normalizes taxonomy, taxon names, publication, institution, specimen/material, occurrence and site-context entities, publishes deterministic inverse indexes, enforces semantic integrity, exposes a deterministic graph projection, and documents append-only migration strategy. Phase 2 adds qualitative claim uncertainty profiles and source-backed interpretation sets without numeric confidence ranking. Phase 3 adds cycle-safe graph traversal (adjacency lookup, breadth-first search, shortest path) and a claim provenance-chain query on top of the existing graph projection. Phase 4 (V25) records each site's dating method and, where a published figure exists, its numeric uncertainty, instead of leaving those fields unset."
  },
